    {
      "date": "2026-02-16",
      "stars": 3,
      "reviewer": "Mandy Zepeda",
      "text": "This is a mixed review.  The store had your typical variety of hispanic fruits and vegetables .Less selection than we can normally find in our local stores but we did find what we needed. We felt like it had a large selection of spices and herbs which we were very happy about. Our main reason for stopping in was the \"pan dulce\" We were very happy with the large selection and quality of the sweet breads. We also bought several bottled drinks which there was a nice selection of. We decided to get a couple of the tacos over at the hot bar just to give it a try. The staff was nice and friendly.  The tacos and salsas were great. The cashier charged me $2.99 for a cup of ice that was in a clear cup so there is no way she didn't know it was just ice that I got to pour one of my bottled drinks I bought in. For the most part it was a good experience.  If we go back to Moore again we would definitely stop back by.",
